WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 8.1 · Marketing & Communications
Communications strategy

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Start from your objectives, not channels, so scarce time goes to the people your start depends on.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:28.133
A communications strategy explains how communication will help you reach your strategic objectives: what people need to know, feel or do, who matters most, what you say, where, with what resources and how you will know.

4
00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:29.133
From objective to measure

5
00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:40.093
Objective: What people need to know, feel or do, linked to a strategic objective. For example: Get one more café to buy bread wholesale every week by June.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:50.311
Audience and message: Who matters most, and what you will say to them. For example: Café owners nearby: fresh bread each morning, baked by trainees they could hire.

7
00:00:50.311 --> 00:01:02.011
Channels and resources: Where you will say it, with the hours, skills and money you really have. For example: Tasting boxes delivered by hand and a follow-up call; four hours a week.

8
00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:12.319
Measure: How you will know it worked: an action you can count. For example: Weekly wholesale orders agreed by the end of June.

9
00:01:12.719 --> 00:01:13.319
Why it matters

10
00:01:13.319 --> 00:01:17.511
1. It stops scarce time going on noise.

11
00:01:17.511 --> 00:01:23.185
2. It focuses on the people whose yes you need to start.

12
00:01:23.185 --> 00:01:29.119
3. It ties communication to what your work must achieve.

13
00:01:29.519 --> 00:01:30.119
What it guides

14
00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:35.422
1. Your audiences, messages and channels, in the lessons that follow.

15
00:01:35.422 --> 00:01:38.874
2. Your campaigns and editorial calendar.

16
00:01:38.874 --> 00:01:44.437
3. Your measurement: each objective gets an outcome measure.

17
00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:45.437
What to avoid

18
00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:49.259
Starting from channels instead of objectives.

19
00:01:49.259 --> 00:01:54.563
Objectives with no audience and no action you can count.

20
00:01:54.563 --> 00:02:00.126
Planning more than the hours you really have.

21
00:02:00.726 --> 00:02:02.526
You write your first communication objectives.

22
00:02:02.526 --> 00:02:06.526
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:08.026 --> 00:02:11.126
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
